DroidWorks U.S.A. – Sensor Fusion Motion Module

Lesson Set 01 | 01_SensorFusion_Motion

Bill of Materials
 Working PIR entry node (/pir_state)
 Working RCWL entry node (/rcwl_state)
 Ubuntu (Linux)
 ROS 2 Jazzy
 Existing droidworks_sensors package

Purpose
This module fuses the two motion sensors (PIR + RCWL) into a single higher-level motion state using the 4-state matrix:
It also provides a simple confidence indication based on sensor agreement.

Create the Node
 Place the node file 06_SensorFusion_Motion into the package
 Add the entry point in setup.py:
  'sensorfusion_motion = droidworks_sensors.sensorfusion_motion:main',

BSR (Build / Source / Run)
 cd ~/droidworks_ws
 colcon build --packages-select droidworks_sensors
 source install/setup.bash
 ros2 run droidworks_sensors sensorfusion_motion

Verify Results
 Bashros2 topic echo /motion_state
 ros2 topic echo /motion_confidence

Expected behavior
 No motion → None + Low/Medium confidence
 Only one sensor triggers → PIR_only or RCWL_only
 Both sensors trigger → Both + High confidence

Success = clean, responsive publications that correctly reflect the combined PIR + RCWL status.
